A||||23||Julian||Engine cleanup for show  - help||||5||
Z||000000||Julian||01-09-2001||11:31 AM||||Anyone have a line on a thread or tips for cleaning up & customising the engine compartment for "show"? (like painting, chrome, custom replacement parts....)<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/meralogo.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||01-09-2001||12:15 PM||||I like mine just stock looking, clean. I dont go in for all the aftermarket goodies like pink looms, etc. I just towell off where I can when I wash it. if Im at a big show, I just spray some WD-40 on everything. Looks all nice n shiney, also keeps stuff from rusting up too (EZ on exhaust parts)||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||01-09-2001||02:24 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=16712481&Sequence=5"> <P>If you have the chance to put the engine together out of the car, then color-matching the engine is a real eye-catcher.  The 2.8 is actually a really flashy looking engine. I have seen blue engines, polished engines. This is mine. I had the plenum and rocker covers powdercoated chrome yellow (very easy to clean), put on the red 8mm Accel wires, and painted the heat shield and cooling tubes with yellow engine paint. The block, heads, and oil pan are also painted to match.  I also just finished polishing my spare throttle body.  The V6-H.O. plate is from a Grand Am.||||reg||1
Z||000003||varnster||01-09-2001||10:47 PM||||TIME, TIME, AND MORE TIME, give your self<BR>plenty. go ahead and replace those vacume hoses while your at it, just be sure one at <BR>a time or label them, took me a little while<BR>to get the cruise working because I didnt <BR>take the time to label, the vacume chart on<BR>the lid is good except for the cruise portion||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||01-10-2001||01:31 AM||||If you get bored and have nothing to do. Just pull a part, clean it up (possibly paint it), and put it back on. I did this on my first Fiero and it improved the looks 1000% by the time I sold it. I just wish that I had taken pictures. It was nothing special, mainly just sanding off rust and repainting stuff black. Then painting the corroded aluminum parts red for contrast. <P>Obviously, if you need anything special to put the part back on,(gaskets etc.) get it before taking it off.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||01-10-2001||12:29 PM||||I agree with detailing before you install it if you can. The color matched blocks and intakes do look nice. I like that ok and repainting anything that needs it. I just think all the neon looms, ect look kinda cheezy. But then beauty is in the eye of the beholder......... Mine looks good from under the hood, but if you crawl under its a dirty, greasy mess. I like driving more than cleaning, lol. btw, stimpy, urs look nice.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 01-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||01-10-2001||02:24 PM||||Thanks. I agree that the neon stuff is a little too fussy for the most part. However SloPonti's Duke looks very sweet with some, well, unorthodox colors. It's all how you work it.  I did use a lot of red wire loom on my engine in places that was unnecessary (cables, vacuum line etc.) but it does add more color for show puposes.  But the main thing is s keep it clean! I think it is a damn crying shame to see someone pop the deck to show off a greasy, dusty engine.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Old Lar||01-10-2001||04:13 PM||||Nolan Concepts makes a lot of chromed parts for the Fiero.  A good quality product.  Not the cheapest cost my any means. Wire looms, air cleaner housing, heat shields cooling tubes for the '87 V6.<P>He is also into powder coating valve covers, intake manifold.||||reg||3
Z||000008||Archie||01-11-2001||02:23 AM||||I HATE cleaning and detailing. I'd rather do 3 nasty V-8 swaps than clean up one car for a show.<P>I have a secret method for cleaning my car up before a show. <P>Now, Don't tell anybody.... Paul Vargyas of the NIFE Club is a real nice guy & LOVES detailing a Fiero. Paul is also very smart and know everything about Fieros. He does a WONDERFUL job as membership director at NIFE. He drives a wonderful car(s), has a wonderful Wife and family. Paul is just a wonderful guy whom also is my personal hero. Paul stops by the shop every once in a while to keep us on the straight and narrow.<P>If anyone happens to talk to Paul in the next week or so, please remind him that the World Of Wheels show is coming up Feb. 2nd. and it would be nice if he could stop by a day or 2 before the show.  ..... Just to visit, mind you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Now, fello Forum Members ^^^ THAT ^^^ is how I get my car cleaned up.<P>Oh, BTW, I'm always looking for more personal heros, so if you have a polishing cloth and know how to use it..... you too can be my personal hero!!!!!<P>Archie  ||||reg||10
Z||000009||Julian||01-11-2001||08:18 AM||||Thanks folks.... the yellow cover is an awsome idea.... my engine is 2 years old..(crate installation from GM) so the top end looks new but it's all the wires & hosed & exhaust that looks old.||||reg||7
Z||000010||TheFiero64||01-11-2001||10:24 AM||||Look at the detail job on this engine. It is Bob Schlag's <B>All I can say is wow</B> <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/images/rlscollage.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieropride.com/images/rlscollage.jpg</A> <P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000011||mshill||01-11-2001||01:00 PM||||Not related to the engine, but I really think the raised wing on the GTs looks much better than the stock low wing.<P>Yeah, that engine compartment is sharp.  That's kind of what I wanted to do with my 86SE, but I couldn't find enaough different sizes of plastic wire looming material in red.  JC Whitless was on backorder.||||reg||14
Z||000012||Alex4mula||01-11-2001||03:23 PM||||PepBoys now sells a chrome one. Looks very nice. Bought it first in Ft. Worth but found it now in FL. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||wkayl||01-11-2001||07:07 PM||||Stock original (except plug wires and dist cap) with STP Son-Of-A-GUN sprayed on the evening befor a show.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cruise6_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Cheever2||01-11-2001||07:34 PM||||Dogbone's lookin a little gnarley there, Wayne.  No, really it's beautiful.  I just saw the other pic's on your site.  Looks superb.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||FieroLisa||01-11-2001||07:34 PM||||Can someone who knows how to use image poster put the pic of my (old) coupes engine (with the gold and purple) on here from <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/86coupe.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierolisa/86coupe.html</A> <BR>Thanks, I miss my car already and its not even gone yet!!<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR>*As Always, Updated Website*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
