Z||000017||Julian||01-12-2001||02:59 PM||||....actually I may just pull the engine out & mount it on an engine stand.  Anyone wanna give me pointers?  I'm not a motorhead so I may just do something stupid..... or if you think I can get to most everything without pulling the engine let me know. Here is a pic of what she looks like now (a bit large in size).... <A HREF="http://homepages.go.com/~mera8071/albums/Mera_Pictures/pic15.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepages.go.com/~mera8071/albums/Mera_Pictures/pic15.html</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000018||Alex4mula||01-12-2001||04:40 PM||||I have used metal polish (California Gold I think) on the unpainted strips on the plenum & valve covers. With a little work you can make them shine almost like a mirror. If they are in bad shape use some fine sanding before the polish. Of course they will look better with a recently painted manifold/cover.||||reg||1
Z||000019||loafer87gt||01-13-2001||01:01 PM||||Be VERY carefull when spraying WD-40 or engine cleaners around your throttle linkage. I was getting my car cleaned up for a show last spring and not knowing any better I lubricated my throttle linkage with WD-40. What I didn't know is that the stuff is like a magnet for dust and grime, and I really bad problems with my throttle sticking.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Mi Junk||01-13-2001||01:53 PM||||What looks real good, is polishing the dog bone. It takes along time to smooth it out and get that mirror look, but worth the effort. Also a Wells Gold dist. cap which is red and has brass term.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mi_junk_sig_2_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000021||speed racer||01-13-2001||04:29 PM||||How do you guys wash the engine with out getting the trunk wet?||||reg||1
